# project: soc2-type-ii-readiness
// SOC 2 Type II readiness: gap assessment -> implement missing controls ->
// three-month observation window with monthly spot-checks -> auditor
// fieldwork with remediation -> report to CEO and sales.

VAR months_observed = 0   // months since the youngest control clock (re)started

=== gap_assessment ===
Assess the current environment against the SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria and produce a prioritized gap list.
Done when every criterion maps to an existing control or a named gap.
* [Gap list complete and prioritized] -> implement_controls

=== implement_controls ===
Implement the missing controls: security tooling, written policies, the onboarding/offboarding process, and the vendor review workflow.
The observation clock does not start until the last control is live.
+ [A control is still being implemented] ~loop~ -> implement_controls
* [Last control is live — observation clock starts] -> observation_window

=== observation_window ===
All controls operating in production; the observation window is running.
The window completes when the youngest control clock reaches three months.
~ months_observed += 1
+ [Month elapsed — run the internal spot-check] -> monthly_spot_check

=== monthly_spot_check ===
Internal spot-check of every control's operation, sampling evidence the way the auditor will.
+ {months_observed < 3} [All controls passing, window not yet complete] ~loop~ -> observation_window
* {months_observed >= 3} [All controls passing and window complete — engage the auditor] @human -> auditor_fieldwork
+ [One or two controls failed] -> control_remediation
+ [Three or more controls failed] -> ciso_window_call

=== ciso_window_call ===
Three or more controls failed this month's spot-check. The CISO decides whether the entire observation window restarts or only the failed controls' clocks.
+ [Restart the entire observation window] @human -> control_remediation
+ [Restart only the failed controls' clocks] @human -> control_remediation

=== control_remediation ===
Fix the failing control(s). A restarted control's clock returns to zero while the other controls keep their elapsed time; the counter tracks the youngest clock.
~ months_observed = 0
+ [Remediated — resume observation] ~loop~ -> observation_window

=== auditor_fieldwork ===
The auditor performs Type II fieldwork over the observation-period evidence.
+ [Findings raised] -> remediate_findings
* [No open findings — report drafted] -> report_distribution

=== remediate_findings ===
Remediate each audit finding and prepare evidence for the auditor's re-test.
+ [Fixes ready for auditor re-test] ~loop~ -> auditor_fieldwork

=== report_distribution ===
The final SOC 2 Type II report is delivered to the CEO, and sales receives it for customer security reviews.
-> END
